I just think it's really cool.

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:06.443
You're also cool too,

00:08:06.443 --> 00:08:07.860
because I know that you've
been a big supporter.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:08.760
You're from New Orleans.
- Right.

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:09.630
- And I think it's really cool

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:11.610
that you're actually
doing something special

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:12.660
with the city, right?

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:13.493
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:08:13.493 --> 00:08:15.720
I partner with GAF

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.360
and we're going around
the southeast regions

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.430
and we're removing blue tarps.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:23.040
So you have all these houses
after the storms come through,

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.740
and they put tarps on the
houses to stop from leaking.

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:28.260
And my dad was a roofer.

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:29.640
I've been doing this
since I was 12-years-old.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:30.590
Believe you me...

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:33.000
It's not fun.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.950
You know, so you get to get up,

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:38.070
go up on these roofs and replace-

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:40.110
give people new roofs after the storms

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:41.910
because there's so many houses

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:43.500
that you fly into the southeast

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:44.850
and it's just blue tarps everywhere.

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:45.840
It's a sea of 'em.

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:48.393
And ironically enough, the
video they just showed,

00:08:49.321 --> 00:08:50.970
I had never met this man before.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:51.850
You know, he was selected
through the process

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:53.610
to do his house.

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.590
Come to find out, he was the dude

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:58.290
who sold my dad the
property to build the house

00:08:58.290 --> 00:08:59.460
that I grew up in.

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:02.007
- What kind of small world was that?

00:09:02.007 --> 00:09:03.420
- And he lives around-

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:05.577
He literally was sitting there like this.

00:09:05.577 --> 00:09:06.900
Right? Not saying nothin'.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.850
He looks at me, he go, "Mackie."

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:09.683
I'm like, "Yeah."

00:09:09.683 --> 00:09:11.760
He go, "You Mackie from
over there by the bridge."

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:12.593
I said, "Yeah."

00:09:12.593 --> 00:09:14.190
He was like, "I sold
your daddy that land."

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:15.150
I'm like, "What?"

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:17.460
And when he told me the whole story

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:19.200
and literally, it blew my mind.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:24.200
Like you never know what
your parents do for you.

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:26.970
You never know the sacrifices they make.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:30.360
The things my dad did for
me to be sitting here.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:32.580
And you know, I kind of joke
about it, and this and that,

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:35.190
but to hear this dude tell this story,

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:38.070
it put the whole GAF
thing into perspective.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:40.140
- And first of all, there's ownership.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.550
I grew up in rentals.

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:43.350
My family, nobody owned anything.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:44.610
So the fact that-

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:47.193
That's an amazing thing, to own something.

00:09:48.594 --> 00:09:49.427
You didn't buy dirt.

00:09:49.427 --> 00:09:50.550
That's not what everybody say happens.

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:52.140
Everybody says, "This house."

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:53.040
- Right.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:55.140
- Your new movie is
called "We Have a Ghost."

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:55.973
I wanna talk about it

00:09:55.973 --> 00:09:58.139
because it's not the typical ghost story.

00:09:58.139 --> 00:09:59.040
Right?

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:00.210
- No, it's different.

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:02.827
It's a ghost with heart.

00:10:02.827 --> 00:10:04.800
So...

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:06.420
This family moves into a house

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:08.910
and they find out that they have a ghost.

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:10.708
And this kid who's kind of like,

00:10:10.708 --> 00:10:13.110
growing through growing pains and puberty,

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:15.000
him and the ghost become friends

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.670
and he goes on this whirlwind
adventure with the ghost

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:20.070
to figure out why this ghost
is stuck in this house.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:21.360
- Yeah, I love that.

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:24.157
Look at that, I did well. (laughs)

00:10:24.157 --> 00:10:27.690
(audience applauds)

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:30.360
So you're from New Orleans

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:31.350
First of all, I love New Orleans.

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:33.330
Anytime we tour there,
it's just a cool city.

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:34.163
I love it.

00:10:34.163 --> 00:10:35.670
So much culture, great food.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:37.980
And great end of tour parties, by the way.

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:40.560
But it's a pretty haunted place though.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.180
There's like some spooky stuff.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:43.013
So growing up there,

00:10:43.013 --> 00:10:44.730
did you ever experience anything?

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:47.640
- No. I will say this,
I do believe in ghosts.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:49.850
My house was built in the 1860s.

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:50.683
- Wow.

00:10:50.683 --> 00:10:53.790
- So when I first moved
in, and my brother,

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:55.950
when he first came to my house,

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.690
like had to renovate
and I'm working in it.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:11:00.000
He comes in, he walks all the
way to the back of the house.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.610
He looks in the yard and
there's a swing in the yard.

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:05.130
And one of the swings is just doing that.

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:06.180
There's no wind.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:07.013
- And no one's in.

00:11:07.013 --> 00:11:08.700
- It just doing that.
- No.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:10.890
- So I come back and I'm
like, "Yo, what'd you doing?"

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:13.500
My brother go, "Caroline on that swing."

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.927
And I'm like, "Why would you say that?"

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:18.390
- Why? Is it her name?

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:19.740
- How do you know her name?

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:21.120
- Oh no.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:22.800
- So we talk and he's standing there.

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:24.570
He keeps looking out the window

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:26.190
like on some Poltergeist-type stuff.

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:27.023
- Yeah, no.

00:11:27.023 --> 00:11:27.990
- So I'm like, "Yo bro, you gotta go.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:28.890
I gotta get back to work."

00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:31.320
So he leaves, he comes back the next week.

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:33.990
And he goes that swing
ain't stop swinging, huh?

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:36.450
Bet, went downstairs, got my saw.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:37.397
Zzzzz.

00:11:37.397 --> 00:11:39.926
(Kelly and audience clapping)

00:11:39.926 --> 00:11:41.010
- Bye-bye, Caroline.

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:42.840
- Bye-bye Caroline, find a new swing.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:43.673
- Oh, my god.

